※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4597

※ What a string is made of is bytes, and what it is encoded as is UTF-8, so the
※ bytes of one are a thing to ask for.  Nothing else in this language has bytes
※ to answer with: an array already is its elements, and a number is a number
※ whatever width it is held in.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let n: u32 = 5u32
    let b: u8⟦⟧ = ⎕bytes(n)
    if #b = 4: 0u6 else: 1u6
